1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,761
New year, new budget?

2
00:00:02,181 --> 00:00:04,538
This year, let's set it up so it actually sticks.

3
00:00:05,308 --> 00:00:12,573
Here's the 2027 money reset: eight things in two parts. Four you do once this week, and four that run all year.

4
00:00:12,993 --> 00:00:15,996
Keep score as we go. How many can you already check off?

5
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,541
Part one. Set it up, this week.

6
00:00:18,961 --> 00:00:19,807
Here's the list.

7
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:26,006
One. Know your take-home pay, per paycheck. Not your salary. The number that actually lands in your account.

8
00:00:26,426 --> 00:00:32,346
Two. Give every bill a paycheck, and even the two checks out, so there's no broke week. That's episode one.

9
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:39,172
Three. List every cost that isn't monthly, and turn it into a small amount per paycheck. That's episode three.

10
00:00:39,592 --> 00:00:45,919
Four. Find the months with three paychecks, and decide now what each extra one will do. That's episode six.

11
00:00:46,689 --> 00:00:48,434
Part two. Let it run, all year.

12
00:00:48,854 --> 00:00:49,751
Here's the rest.

13
00:00:50,171 --> 00:00:58,078
Five. List every debt, pick snowball or avalanche, and send every extra dollar at one target. Episode two ran the numbers.

14
00:00:58,498 --> 00:01:03,595
Six. Build a starter emergency fund, so one flat tire doesn't land on a credit card.

15
00:01:04,015 --> 00:01:10,797
Seven. Automate it. Bills, sinking funds and savings all move on payday, without you deciding every time.

16
00:01:11,217 --> 00:01:15,931
And eight. Fifteen minutes, every other Sunday. Check the balances, and adjust one thing.

17
00:01:16,351 --> 00:01:24,456
For the emergency fund, a simple first goal is one month of bills. In our example from episode one, that's $2,371.

18
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:28,536
Reach it faster by sending one of your three-paycheck months straight there.

19
00:01:28,956 --> 00:01:31,445
And the money check-in only needs three questions.

20
00:01:31,865 --> 00:01:36,329
Did every bill get paid? What surprised you? And how much closer is the target?

21
00:01:36,749 --> 00:01:42,262
So, what's your score out of eight? Put it in the comments. Zero is a perfectly good place to start.

22
00:01:43,032 --> 00:01:50,596
The Paycheck Planner in the description covers the first five in one file: bills, surprise funds, paydays, and your debt-free date.

23
00:01:51,016 --> 00:01:52,718
Subscribe, and happy new year.
